    For the non-heading-up case, the normal path should invalidate the area; if we return early without, the display won't update until the finish whole-C invalidate. The finish has `if (!heading_up) lv_obj_invalidate(canvas)`, so the final frame updates. Intermediate progress is less smooth but fine. To keep it simple, the early return as written is acceptable (the final frame updates C when heading_up false; when heading_up true, C is hidden or frozen briefly).
