While waiting, reconsider the early return's effect on the **visible C refresh during a non-heading-up keep-pan**:
- render_begin full_restamp true; C visible (heading_up false). Pump draws tiles; `vmap_view_invalidate_canvas_area` returns early → no LVGL invalidation per tile. At render_finish: `stamp_overlays`; then `if (!heading_up) lv_obj_clear_flag(canvas, HIDDEN)`; bottom `if (!heading_up) lv_obj_invalidate(canvas)` → whole C invalidated once. The display updates at the end. The repaint takes ~200ms; the user sees the old C frozen then updates. Acceptable.
- For heading_up transition, C visible; per-tile invalidations skipped; at finish, the switch hides C/shows R; R invalidated by `vmap_rot_full`; display updates. If pending not ready (restamp interrupted), C stays visible and no per-tile invalidation → C may not show the partial repaint; but the finish's bottom (heading_up true) doesn't invalidate C. The service C-visible branch invalidates C every 5Hz (if called), so eventually. If no service, C frozen until the next event. The restamp usually completes; if it fails, a retry. Fine.
- The early return also skips the **rot_pending** marking for external changes during the restamp; the restamp covers all C; overlays stamped at finish; okay.

